<div class="content-page">
  <div class="content-page__inner">
    <h1 class="content-page__title">Features</h1>
    <p class="content-page__intro">Everything Math Direct includes, and why each part is there.</p>

    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">{{ program.lessons.length }} scripted lessons</h2>
      <p>Pre-K, Kindergarten, and First Grade, plus an optional Bridge to Second Grade. Every step gives the words to say, what to do, the answer to expect, and the correction to give. New skills are shown, done together, and then done alone.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Skill tracks with spaced review</h2>
      <p>Each lesson draws short exercises from several skills. A new step is firmed for two lessons and then reviewed at widening intervals, so nothing is learned once and forgotten. The <a href="/curriculum/">scope and sequence</a> shows every step.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Firm and Error marking</h2>
      <p>The parent marks each answer. An error brings up the correction and lets you start the exercise over. Missed items come back at the end of the lesson, and the lesson ends with advice to go on, reteach, or repeat.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Mastery tests and a placement test</h2>
      <p>A test after every tenth lesson checks each skill and lists the exercises to reteach for any part not passed. The placement test finds the right starting lesson.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">A screen made for young children</h2>
      <p>The child's screen shows only large numbers and pictures, never words to read. Children answer aloud or by touching. Dots can be shown for a moment to build quick recognition of small amounts, and numbers can be shown being written stroke by stroke.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Worksheets and materials</h2>
      <p>Every lesson in Kindergarten, First Grade, and the Bridge has a printable worksheet with an optional answer key; Pre-K worksheets are optional. Number cards, dot cards, ten-frames, shape cards, a tens-and-ones mat, and a clock face are on the <a href="/materials/">materials page</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Practice and fact review</h2>
      <p><a href="/practice/">Practice</a> for any skill, drawn only from what the child has been taught. A <a href="/facts/">fact review</a> that brings missed facts back first and records when each fact becomes firm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">A teacher dashboard</h2>
      <p>For each child: the placement result, progress in each level, test results, the skills where errors cluster, recent lessons, a chart of which facts are firm, and notes. It prints as a report.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Private, free, and offline</h2>
      <p>No accounts, no tracking, and no advertising. Records stay in the browser and can be saved to a file. Lessons you have opened keep working without a connection.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-page__cta">
      <a href="/lessons/" class="btn btn--cta">See the lessons</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
